x86_64-linux  The C1 and D1 forms of three implicit special members - `_ZN3TwoC1Ev`, `_ZN3TwoC1ERKS_`, `_ZN3TwoD1Ev` and the same three for `Mixed` and `Three`. clang emits only the base-object C2 and D2 forms of a constructor and destructor it writes itself on this target and calls those directly, where cxx1 emits the complete-object forms beside them: identical bodies for a class with no virtual base, mergeable definitions both, so the cost is object size. The same fact move-constructor.nonames and reference-temporary-lifetime.nonames record. These three cannot be defined out of line the way those cases answer it - the compiler writes them - and every name the case is about agrees: `_ZN1EC1Ev`, `_ZN1EC1ERKS_`, `_ZN1ED1Ev` and `_Z3sumRA2_A3_K1E`, whose two array dimensions are exactly what this measures. x86_64-windows and arm64-darwin agree with clang name for name.
